course: dictionary
lesson: 2508
title: Deceive and looks can deceive
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To deceive someone means to make them believe something that is not true, so they will be tricked. Look at the words around it for clues. If a message is trying to get you to believe a lie, it is trying to deceive you.
explain: «Looks can deceive» is a useful saying. Something can look one way but really be another. A shiny offer on a screen might look safe, but it could be a trick.
explain: You can also deceive yourself. That means you refuse to believe a truth you do not like, even when the evidence is there. «Do not be deceived» is a warning: do not let yourself be fooled.
fact: Deceive is a verb. Its forms are deceive, deceives, deceived and deceiving.
fact: «Deceive» means to make someone believe something that is not true, in order to trick them.
fact: «Deceived» is the past form: «The fake message deceived him into sharing his password.»
fact: To deceive yourself means to refuse to believe a truth you don't like.
fact: Honesty means telling the truth and not deceiving others, even when a lie seems easier.
exercise: «The fake email tried to deceive Sam into sharing his password.» What does deceive mean here? | *To trick someone into believing something untrue | To hurry someone along | To send a friendly letter to a friend | To read something aloud to a class
exercise: «Looks can deceive.» What does this saying mean? | *Things can seem one way but be another | People with dark hair are clever | Mirrors always tell the truth | Pretty things are always good
exercise: Which example shows someone deceiving themselves? | Cooking a meal for the family | Running very fast in a race | Telling a joke to make friends laugh | *Refusing to believe a truth they do not like
test: «The trickster deceived the villagers.» Which word shows that the deceiving happened in the past? | *deceived | the | trickster | villagers
test: «Honesty means telling the truth and not deceiving others.» Which choice is the opposite of deceiving? | *Telling the truth | Making up a story | Pretending to be someone else | Tricking a friend
exam: Which sentence shows someone deceiving another person? | The dog wagged its tail when it saw the ball | The sun rose early over the green hills | She wrote a thank-you card to her grandmother | *The thief pretended to be a police officer to get into the house
